{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "example2-training-bundle",
      "prompt": "Build the local Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer training bundle from the Hugging Face example2 sample, the data preparation step of the skill's Stage 0 to 3 walkthrough, and stop there: no checkpoint conversion and no training. The sample is not bundled in the skill: the documented preparation downloads it from the model's Hugging Face repository (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer, assets/sample_data/example2), and the bundle step downloads the Nano text tokenizer (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano, text_tokenizer only). Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill, and set it up per the skill. Use outputs/ as the workflow's destination directory (SIM_TRANSFER_OUTPUT), so that the prepared training row is outputs/training.jsonl, the bundle is outputs/training-bundle and the preparation summary that the bundle script reports is outputs/training-bundle.summary.json. Record the number of prepared clips, the exclusions and the bundle's file list in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "scripts/paibench_local_bundle.py prepare-custom builds outputs/training-bundle from the one example2 row of outputs/training.jsonl (manifest.json, samples.json with the example2 record, the tokenizer resources and the source media), and outputs/training-bundle.summary.json reports status prepared with 1 sample, with result_summary.md recording the commands, the prepared and excluded counts and the wall time.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Framework training environment was installed from the lockfile of the checkout that contains this skill, as the skill's setup documents (Python 3.13, uv 0.11.29, all extras with the cu130-train group, or cu128-train for CUDA 12.8), and the preparation commands ran from that environment, not the system python",
        "The example2 sample was downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer revision main (assets/sample_data/example2) and the Sim-Transfer inference skill's scripts/prepare_hf_sample.py --example example2 wrote outputs/training.jsonl with the one example2 row (identity example2, caption_start 0, caption_end 121)",
        "The Nano text tokenizer was downloaded with the documented hf download command (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano, revision e59a53c25979a090fa8706c9acc0c254a6e89b92, text_tokenizer/*) and the bundle was built in a new directory with this skill's scripts/paibench_local_bundle.py prepare-custom (--manifest, --tokenizer, --output, --dataset-name sim_transfer_example2), as references/local-dataset.md documents",
        "outputs/training-bundle holds manifest.json and samples.json, samples.json has exactly one record, with identity example2 and an assets mapping for the RGB, depth and segmentation media retained in the bundle, and outputs/training-bundle.summary.json reports status prepared and samples 1",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the bundle and its summary trace to a real prepare-custom run in the transcript, no checkpoint was converted and no training was started, and result_summary.md records the exact commands, the prepared and excluded counts and the wall time actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/training.jsonl",
          "contains": "\"identity\": \"example2\""
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/training-bundle/manifest.json",
          "contains": "structured_93_dense_7"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/training-bundle/samples.json",
          "contains": "\"identity\": \"example2\""
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/training-bundle.summary.json",
          "contains": "\"status\": \"prepared\""
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "example2 download + training row",
        "tokenizer + bundle build",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nano-conversion-preflight",
      "prompt": "Before any model weights are downloaded, check that this framework checkout and its environment can run the skill's pinned Cosmos3-Nano to DCP conversion: run the converter and runtime check of the skill's Nano conversion reference (its check-env step) and stop there. Do not download or convert the model. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill, and set it up per the skill. Save the JSON that the check prints as outputs/nano_check_env.json and record the Framework revision and the package versions it reports in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "scripts/prepare_nano_dcp.py check-env exits 0 from the Framework environment of the checkout and outputs/nano_check_env.json holds the JSON it printed (framework_revision, python and the installed cosmos-framework, torch, transformers, huggingface-hub and tokenizers versions), with no model weights downloaded and result_summary.md recording the command, the reported revision and versions and the wall time.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Framework training environment was installed from the lockfile of the checkout that contains this skill, as the skill's setup documents (Python 3.13, uv 0.11.29, all extras with the cu130-train group, or cu128-train for CUDA 12.8), and the check ran from that environment, not the system python",
        "The check was run from the Framework checkout root as references/nano-conversion.md documents (this skill's scripts/prepare_nano_dcp.py check-env --framework-dir \"$FRAMEWORK_DIR\"), it exited 0 and printed no line starting with 'Nano conversion check failed'",
        "outputs/nano_check_env.json is the JSON the check printed: framework_revision equals the commit that git rev-parse HEAD reports for the checkout, and python, cosmos-framework, torch, transformers, huggingface-hub and tokenizers each carry a version",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated and nothing beyond the check ran: the JSON traces to a real check-env run in the transcript, the convert step was not started, no Cosmos3-Nano weights were downloaded, and result_summary.md records the exact command, the reported revision and versions and the wall time actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/nano_check_env.json",
          "contains": "\"framework_revision\""
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "converter and runtime check",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stage0-resolve-dryrun",
      "prompt": "Take the skill's Stage 0 quickstart for Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer as far as its dry run, without training: build the example2 training bundle, convert the pinned Cosmos3-Nano weights (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano, the revision the skill pins) to DCP with the skill's conversion helper, download the video VAE the skill names, bind the local resources, write the Stage 0 arguments with the skill's stage helper and run the documented dry run of the Stage 0 command. Do not start torchrun training. The sample is not bundled in the skill: the documented preparation downloads example2 from the model's Hugging Face repository (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer, assets/sample_data/example2). Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill, and set it up per the skill. Use outputs/ as the example2 workflow's destination directory (SIM_TRANSFER_OUTPUT), so that the bundle is outputs/training-bundle and its preparation summary is outputs/training-bundle.summary.json; keep the Nano download, the converted DCP and the training output root in a working directory outside the artifacts. Copy the conversion receipt (nano_conversion.json in the DCP root) to outputs/nano_conversion.json, the arguments file that the stage helper wrote to outputs/stage0.args and the config.yaml that the dry run wrote to outputs/stage0_config.yaml. The skill asks for 160 GiB of host memory for the conversion, which runs on CPU. After the bundle is built, compare this host's total memory with that figure: if the host has less, that measured comparison is the blocker: record both numbers in result_summary.md, do not download or convert the Nano weights and stop there. If the host has enough, make a genuine attempt at every remaining step and, if one fails, record the exact command, its error and the measured memory and disk numbers. Never fabricate a receipt, an arguments file or a config.yaml.",
      "expected_outcome": "On a host with the 160 GiB of host memory the skill asks for, scripts/prepare_nano_dcp.py convert produces a verified DCP of the pinned nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano snapshot, scripts/qa_transfer_stage.py --stage 0 writes the sim_local_transfer_stage0_bidir arguments for the example2 bundle and the --dryrun of cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment writes config.yaml in the run's _stage0 folder under cosmos3_sim_transfer/local, with the receipt, the arguments file and config.yaml copied to outputs/; only on a host with less memory does result_summary.md instead document that measured blocker.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Framework training environment was installed from the lockfile of the checkout that contains this skill, as the skill's setup documents (Python 3.13, uv 0.11.29, all extras with the cu130-train group, or cu128-train for CUDA 12.8), and the example2 bundle was built at outputs/training-bundle with this skill's scripts/paibench_local_bundle.py prepare-custom as references/local-dataset.md documents, with outputs/training-bundle.summary.json reporting status prepared",
        "The host's total memory was measured and compared with the 160 GiB of host memory that references/nano-conversion.md asks for before any Nano weights were downloaded; on a host with less, result_summary.md documents that blocker with both numbers and the conversion was not started",
        "If the host had the memory: the pinned nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano snapshot (revision e59a53c25979a090fa8706c9acc0c254a6e89b92) was converted on CPU with this skill's scripts/prepare_nano_dcp.py as references/nano-conversion.md documents (check-env, then convert with --framework-dir, --source-dir and --output-dir on two new directories), the helper ended with its line 'Verified pinned Nano conversion and checkpoint file hashes; training compatibility remains unchecked.', the DCP root holds model/.metadata and model/config.json, and outputs/nano_conversion.json is the receipt from that root",
        "If the host had the memory: the local resources were bound as SKILL.md '1. Bind local resources' documents (TRANSFER_BUNDLE_PATH the example2 bundle, BASE_CKPT_ROOT the converted DCP, VIDEO_VAE_PATH the Wan2.2_VAE.pth of Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B at revision 921dbaf3f1674a56f47e83fb80a34bac8a8f203e, the two audio assets under $NANO_HF_DIR/sound_tokenizer, TRANSFER_QA_BASE_MODEL_ONLY=1), outputs/stage0.args is the file that python \"$STAGE_HELPER\" --stage 0 wrote and names experiment=sim_local_transfer_stage0_bidir, and outputs/stage0_config.yaml is the config.yaml that python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --dryrun with trainer.max_iter=6 wrote under $IMAGINAIRE_OUTPUT_ROOT/cosmos3_sim_transfer/local/ in the run's _stage0 folder",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated and no training was started: every file under outputs/ traces to a real run in the transcript, torchrun was not launched, and result_summary.md records the commands, the measured host memory, the wall time of each step and the paths actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/training-bundle.summary.json",
          "contains": "\"status\": \"prepared\""
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "example2 bundle",
        "Nano conversion or blocker analysis",
        "Stage 0 arguments + dry run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 90,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
